[162.67667, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline & Configuration Weakness Report\n\n## Overview\nAnalysis of system configuration files on host `redis-prod-01` revealed multiple critical baseline security deficiencies that enabled initial compromise, execution, lateral escalation, and persistent evasion.\n\n## Identified Baseline Weaknesses\n\n### 1. Insecure Redis Service Baseline (BAS-01 / CHK-05)\n- **Configuration File**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`\n- **Current Setting**: `Redis protected-mode no; bind 0.0.0.0; no password set`\n- **Baseline Deviation**: CIS / Debian Security Baseline requires:\n  1. `bind 127.0.0.1` (or binding strictly to private internal management interfaces).\n  2. `protected-mode yes`.\n  3. Robust authentication enabled via `requirepass <strong_password>`.\n  4. Disabling or renaming dangerous administrative commands (`CONFIG`, `FLUSHALL`, `SAVE`, `EVAL`).\n- **Severity**: **CRITICAL**.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`, `/sas/baseline.json:1`, `/sas/alerts.json` (ALERT-03).\n\n### 2. Unrestricted Dynamic Linker Hijacking Vulnerability\n- **Configuration File**: `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`\n- **Current Setting**: File present referencing userland rootkit library `/lib/.hide.so` (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`).\n- **Baseline Deviation**: `/etc/ld.so.preload` should not exist or must be empty and strictly monitored by File Integrity Monitoring (FIM).\n- **Severity**: **HIGH**.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`.\n\n### 3. Weak SSH Daemon Security & Authentication Baseline\n- **Log Evidence**: `/disk/var/log/auth.log:176`, `/disk/var/log/auth.log:208`\n- **Current Setting**: Direct root password login permitted (`PermitRootLogin yes`), password-based authentication enabled, and no connection rate-limiting tool (e.g., `fail2ban`).\n- **Baseline Deviation**: SSH security policy requires disabling root password login (`PermitRootLogin prohibit-password` or `no`), enforcing public-key authentication (`PasswordAuthentication no`), and implementing brute-force protection.\n- **Severity**: **HIGH**.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/var/log/auth.log:208`.\n\n### 4. Insecure Mount Options on World-Writable Directories\n- **Directory**: `/tmp` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:1`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1`)\n- **Current Setting**: Executable binaries and shared libraries executed directly out of `/tmp`.\n- **Baseline Deviation**: `/tmp` and `/var/tmp` must be mounted on dedicated filesystems with `noexec`, `nosuid`, and `nodev` mount flags in `/etc/fstab` (`/disk/etc/fstab:1`).\n- **Severity**: **MEDIUM**.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:1`, `/disk/etc/fstab:1`.\nEOF\n"]
