[162.682817, "o", "- **Current Setting**: Direct root password login permitted (`PermitRootLogin yes`), password-based authentication enabled, and no connection rate-limiting tool (e.g., `fail2ban`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Baseline Deviation**: SSH security policy requires disabling root password login (`PermitRootLogin prohibit-password` or `no`), enforcing public-key authentication (`PasswordAuthentication no`), and implementing brute-force protection.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Severity**: **HIGH**.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/var/log/auth.log:208`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 4. Insecure Mount Options on World-Writable Directories\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Directory**: `/tmp` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:1`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Current Setting**: Executable binaries and shared libraries executed directly out of `/tmp`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Baseline Deviation**: `/tmp` and `/var/tmp` must be mounted on dedicated filesystems with `noexec`, `nosuid`, and `nodev` mount flags in `/etc/fstab` (`/disk/etc/fstab:1`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Severity**: **MEDIUM**.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:1`, `/disk/etc/fstab:1`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
